-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA SNAPSHOT — generated from the live production database
-- (lrstswfxfsezdmvkvukc), regenerated 2026-10-25 (test/regression), replacing
-- the 2026-08-03 snapshot that predated PARTYSTAGING, ADDITEM, NOSTRIP,
-- BUYANDBOOK, CATEGORISE, SLOTREACH and LESSONPLAN. This is the test harness's
-- setup path (Task 4, hardening-unit-spec addendum), not the migration chain.
--
-- WHY: createTestDb() previously replayed all migration files in order
-- against a fresh PGlite instance. That chain has a real, load-bearing break
-- (20260709160000_enforce_launch_modules.sql: FK violation on org_modules,
-- because a later migration's seed insert assumes an org row that a fresh
-- replay hasn't created at that point in history) — every test/db/*.test.ts
-- file has therefore never actually run against that path. This snapshot
-- sidesteps the whole class of "migration N assumes migration M's insert
-- already happened with a specific row" bugs by capturing the live
-- database's ACTUAL current state directly, instead of replaying history.
--
-- ADDITIVE ONLY: no existing migration file is modified, renamed, or deleted.
-- The migration chain still exists, in full, for provenance and for direct
-- production deploys — this snapshot is a second, independent input, used
-- only by the test harness (test/db/harness.ts).
--
-- ⚠️ ~31 migrations in this repo REWRITE existing function bodies in place
-- (CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION reissues matching an "anchor" body) and are NOT
-- safe to replay on a fresh database — on a fresh PGlite there is no prior
-- body to match, so the rewrite finds nothing and silently no-ops. This
-- snapshot path sidesteps that entire class by dumping the LIVE function
-- bodies directly (pg_dump emits each function's CURRENT definition, not the
-- migration history that produced it) — so every in-place rewrite is already
-- baked in, correctly, with no replay involved. This is a pre-existing
-- property of the repo (recorded since the original Task 4 snapshot), not
-- something this regeneration needed to fix.
--
-- CONTENTS:
--   1. Full `public` schema — every type, table, function, trigger, index,
--      view, and RLS policy — SCHEMA ONLY (no rows) for every table except
--      the fourteen named below. `auth`/`storage` are NOT included here; the
--      harness's own BOOTSTRAP block (harness.ts) continues to emulate those
--      minimally, unchanged.
--   2. Seed DATA (rows) for exactly fourteen tables — pure product
--      configuration + global/single-tenant lookups, matching
--      SNAPSHOT_DATA_TABLES in harness.ts, each previously reviewed for PII
--      (no new tables added in this regeneration):
--        - organizations       (1 row — the tenant: id/name/slug/status only)
--        - service_types       (pure catalog lookup)
--        - contract_templates
--        - contract_section_defs
--        - contract_clause_defs
--        - contract_field_defs
--        - template_tokens
--        - modules / tiers / tier_modules   (global platform catalog)
--        - horse_breeds / horse_colors      (global vocabulary)
--        - org_modules          (tenant #1's module entitlements — the one
--                                 per-tenant table here, module keys +
--                                 booleans only, no personal data)
--        - template_variants    (global contract-variant registry)
--      No other table's rows are included. business_config remains
--      EXCLUDED: it carries a real person's name (signatory_name) and a live
--      FK into contacts (signatory_contact_id) — real PII.
--
-- DRIFT GUARD: harness.ts's SNAPSHOT_DATA_TABLES set + snapshotDataTargets()
-- assert that no INSERT statement in this file targets a table outside the
-- fourteen named above; createTestDbFromSnapshot() throws before ever loading
-- the file if that's violated. If a future regeneration of this snapshot
-- picks up rows for a fifteenth table, the harness setup fails loudly instead
-- of silently absorbing whatever that table happens to contain. Changing the
-- allowed table list is a deliberate, reviewed edit to SNAPSHOT_DATA_TABLES in
-- harness.ts — never an accidental side effect of regenerating this file.
--
-- HOW THIS WAS GENERATED (for the next regeneration):
--   DBURL=$(cat .env.db)
--   pg_dump "$DBURL" --schema-only --schema=public --no-owner --no-privileges \
--     --no-tablespaces -f schema-only.sql
--   pg_dump "$DBURL" --data-only --column-inserts --disable-triggers \
--     --no-owner --no-privileges \
--     --table=public.organizations --table=public.service_types \
--     --table=public.contract_templates --table=public.contract_section_defs \
--     --table=public.contract_clause_defs --table=public.contract_field_defs \
--     --table=public.template_tokens --table=public.modules \
--     --table=public.tiers --table=public.tier_modules \
--     --table=public.horse_breeds --table=public.horse_colors \
--     --table=public.org_modules --table=public.template_variants \
--     -f data-only.sql
--   Then: strip pg_dump 18's `\restrict`/`\unrestrict` meta-commands (PGlite's
--   psql-less exec() does not understand them) and comment out `CREATE SCHEMA
--   public;` (PGlite already has one), and concatenate schema-only + data-only
--   under this header. harness.ts's own `SET search_path TO public;` / `SET
--   row_security = on;` calls after loading handle the two session-scoped
--   settings pg_dump's own header leaves behind (search_path='', row_security
--   =off) — see createTestDbFromSnapshot()'s comments for why those two lines
--   are enforced in code rather than trusted to survive in the dump alone.
--   ⚠️ `--disable-triggers` is now REQUIRED on the data-only dump (added this
--   regeneration): contract_templates gained a self-referencing FK
--   (companion_template_key -> contract_templates.template_key, migration
--   20260811T1700_oneauthor_template_surface_config.sql) since the last
--   snapshot. Plain sequential INSERTs now fail
--   ("contract_templates_companion_fkey" violated) whenever a companion row
--   is inserted before the template it points at. pg_dump warns about this
--   circular-FK case itself and names the fix; --disable-triggers wraps the
--   table's data in `ALTER TABLE ... DISABLE/ENABLE TRIGGER ALL`, which needs
--   owner/superuser privilege — the connection loading this file has it. If a
--   future regeneration adds MORE circular self-references, expect the same
--   fix to keep working; if pg_dump ever refuses outright, the fallback is
--   `ALTER TABLE ... ADD CONSTRAINT ... DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED` at
--   restore time, or a second pass of `UPDATE` statements after all rows load.
-- ============================================================================

